task: codec-jsonschema-refinement-enum
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/codec-jsonschema-refinement-enum
worktree: ../okay-wt-enum

why: intent-structured-output found the derived JSON schema renders a
  refinement (`Conf`, `Schema.refine` over a string) as a plain
  string, so a response_format contract or a tool declaration cannot
  carry the vocabulary a prompt has to state. A tool parameter that
  is an enum should be an enum in the declaration Claude/OpenAI see.

what: `Schema.enumeration[A, B](values, name)` — a refinement over a
  finite vocabulary: on every wire it is `refine` (the name goes
  out, the name comes back, an unknown one is a decode error naming
  the vocabulary); in `JsonSchema.of` it is the underlying type plus
  `"enum": [...]`. Carried as a second parameter list on `SIso`
  (`vocabulary: Option[Vector[B]]`), so the twenty `SIso(u, to, from)`
  patterns across the algebras stay as they are and only the
  declaration reads it. `Conf` becomes an enumeration. Tests: the
  wire is unchanged, the schema carries the enum, a plain refine does
  not, an integer vocabulary declares integers — JVM, JS, Native.
